.TH ARMYBOX-INIT 8 "2026-02-08" "armybox 0.3.0" "ArmyBox Manual"
.\"
.SH NAME
armybox init \- system initialization process (PID\ 1)
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B init
.br
.B linuxrc
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B init
is the first process started by the Linux kernel after mounting the root
filesystem.
It runs as PID\ 1 and is responsible for:
.IP \(bu 2
Executing system startup scripts
.IP \(bu 2
Spawning login terminals (via
.BR getty (8))
.IP \(bu 2
Adopting orphaned processes
.IP \(bu 2
Handling system shutdown and reboot
.PP
The
.B armybox
init system is a lightweight, BusyBox-compatible init implementation
that reads its configuration from
.BR /etc/inittab .
.PP
When invoked as
.BR linuxrc ,
init performs the same role but is intended for use within an initramfs,
where it can perform early setup before pivoting to the real root filesystem.
.\"
.SH STARTUP SEQUENCE
.TP
.B 1.
Set up signal handlers and become session leader.
.TP
.B 2.
If
.I /etc/inittab
exists, parse it and execute entries with the
.B sysinit
action.
.TP
.B 3.
Execute entries with the
.B wait
action (blocking until each completes).
.TP
.B 4.
Execute entries with the
.B once
action (non-blocking).
.TP
.B 5.
For each
.B respawn
entry, fork and exec the specified process.
If a respawned process exits, init will restart it after a brief delay.
.TP
.B 6.
Enter the main loop: wait for child processes and respawn them as needed.
.\"
.SH SHUTDOWN SEQUENCE
When init receives
.B SIGTERM
(sent by
.BR reboot (8),
.BR halt (8),
or
.BR poweroff (8)):
.TP
.B 1.
Execute entries with the
.B shutdown
action.
.TP
.B 2.
Send
.B SIGTERM
to all processes.
.TP
.B 3.
Wait briefly, then send
.B SIGKILL
to remaining processes.
.TP
.B 4.
Unmount filesystems and halt/reboot/power off.
.\"
.SH INITTAB FORMAT
.I /etc/inittab
consists of lines in the format:
.PP
.RS
.IB id : runlevels : action : process
.RE
.PP
Fields:
.TP
.I id
A unique identifier for the entry (1\(en4 characters).
Typically the tty name (e.g.,
.BR tty1 ,
.BR ttyS0 ).
.TP
.I runlevels
Ignored by armybox (compatibility field).
.TP
.I action
One of:
.RS
.TP
.B sysinit
Run during system initialization, before any other entries.
.TP
.B wait
Run once and wait for completion.
.TP
.B once
Run once without waiting.
.TP
.B respawn
Start the process and restart it whenever it exits.
.TP
.B askfirst
Like
.BR respawn ,
but print \(lqPlease press Enter to activate this console\(rq
and wait for a keypress before starting.
.TP
.B shutdown
Run during system shutdown.
.TP
.B restart
Run when init receives
.BR SIGHUP .
.TP
.B ctrlaltdel
Run when Ctrl+Alt+Delete is pressed.
.RE
.TP
.I process
The command to execute, including arguments.
.\"
.SH EXAMPLE INITTAB
.PP
.nf
# System initialization
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -o remount,rw /
::sysinit:/bin/hostname -F /etc/hostname

# Run system startup script
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# Virtual console TTYs
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
tty2::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty2

# Serial console
ttyS0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 115200 ttyS0 vt100

# Ctrl-Alt-Delete
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Shutdown
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcK
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
.fi
.\"
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read
.I /etc/inittab
and execute
.B restart
entries.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Begin the shutdown sequence.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Close and re-open the console device.
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/inittab
Init configuration file.
See
.BR inittab (5).
.TP
.I /etc/init.d/rcS
System startup script (typically invoked via
.B sysinit
action).
.TP
.I /etc/init.d/rcK
System shutdown script (typically invoked via
.B shutdown
action).
.TP
.I /dev/console
Default console device.
.\"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR armybox (1),
.BR inittab (5),
.BR getty (8),
.BR halt (8),
.BR reboot (8),
.BR poweroff (8),
.BR switch_root (8),
